0..73 Comment "// Substitution whose lifting is a definition rather than the constructor"
74..138 Comment "// `Lift`, beside `subst-subst`\'s `substTwiceUnderLam`. Two such"
139..213 Comment "// substitutions at an abstraction unfold the outer one at the inner one\'s"
214..284 Comment "// stuck call, beside the lifting call that unfolds to `Lift`; the two"
285..362 Comment "// recursive calls compare part by part, so the step converts as it does with"
363..388 Comment "// lifting a constructor."
389..391 Comment "//"
392..406 Comment "// - see: #879"
